  "apparatus": "Type-I down-conversion, heralded polarization preparation, HWPs and birefringent beam-displacer shifts. The paper reports 0.992 interference visibility per step, 7 ns coincidence window and APD dark rate below 100/s. These do not determine accidental coincidences or relative collection efficiencies.",
  "model": "Keep the published HWP field matrix. Within each mixing pair, redistribute its incoming mass in proportion to the output absolute amplitudes to the chosen power; identity propagation carries mass unchanged. The prepared spinor is cos(phi/2) H +/- sin(phi/2) V, implemented with PBS and HWP. For x=3 the local shares multiply. Evaluated at the tabulated physical settings with no fitted parameters for nominal predictions. The fitted odds ratio, odds range 0.8..1.2, independent +/-1-degree plate errors and <=1% contamination are separate sensitivity examples, not measured bounds.",
  "limits": "The inconclusive arm does not recombine at the third tick. The comparison tests a quartic extension to the calibrated nonbalanced polarization rotations, including a version using Born-prepared weights. A rule specified only for balanced Hadamard mixing with no stated response for other angles is underdetermined here. Interference visibility is not the only possible imperfection. Angle-dependent detection losses or altered Jones amplitudes could change the comparison."
